---
name: refresh-maps
description: |-
  Refresh the box's MAP.md files. Each directory in the box has a MAP.md
  listing its immediate children with one-line annotations; this procedure
  keeps that listing accurate as files and directories are added or
  removed. Plain edits to existing files do not trigger updates.

  The precheck exits with CHECK_SKIP when no immediate-children set has
  changed since the last refresh, so on quiet days this procedure does
  no work and invokes no agent.
steps:
  - id: refresh
    description: Identify dirty MAP.md files and rewrite them with current annotated
      listings
    precheck:
      shells:
        - |-
          cb refresh-maps
          # cb refresh-maps exits CHECK_SKIP_CODE (75) when there's nothing
          # to do, or when the box is in an unworkable state (uncommitted
          # work, not a git repo, no commits yet).
      whys:
        - |-
          No need to invoke an agent if no immediate-children sets have
          changed since the last refresh.
    run:
      agents:
        - prompt: |-
            You are refreshing the box's MAP.md index files.

            Each directory in the box has (or should have) a MAP.md that lists
            its immediate children with one-line annotations. CLAUDE.md
            @-imports MAP.md so agents working in the box see the listing.

            STEP 1 - GET THE BRIEF:
            ```
            cb refresh-maps --brief
            ```
            This prints a JSON brief with one task per MAP.md that needs work:

            ```json
            {
              "needsWork": true,
              "head": "<commit-hash>",
              "tasks": [
                {
                  "map": "inbox/MAP.md",
                  "dir": "inbox",
                  "action": "update",
                  "asOf": "<previous-commit>",
                  "head": "<commit-hash>",
                  "added": ["new.card", "triage/"],
                  "deleted": ["old.card"],
                  "children": ["bar.card", "new.card", "triage/"]
                }
              ]
            }
            ```

            - `action: "create"` — MAP.md is missing. Write a fresh one
              covering all entries in `children`.
            - `action: "update"` — MAP.md already exists. Read it, then add
              lines for `added` items and remove lines for `deleted` items.
              Preserve annotations for unchanged entries.

            STEP 2 - WRITE EACH MAP.md:

            MAP.md is primarily a directory index. List subdirectories, not
            every file. Only mention files when they anchor the directory:
            briefing cards (`*.briefing.card`), `README.md`, landmark cards
            (`*.landmark.card`), or top-level docs. Don't enumerate per-item
            card files, attachments, or generated files — the parent's
            listing already names this dir, and an `ls` shows contents
            directly.

            Format:

            ```
            # Map: <dir-path>

            - `subdir/` — what kind of contents this subdir holds
            - `self-explanatory-name/`
            - `briefing.briefing.card` — context for this area (only if present)
            ```

            Rules for annotations:
            - Annotations are OPTIONAL. If the filename or directory name is
              already self-explanatory (e.g. `2024/`, `recipes/`, `README.md`,
              a person's name), just list it as a bare bullet — no ` — …`.
              The annotation only earns its place when it tells a reader
              something the name doesn't.
            - When you do annotate: ≤ 100 characters.
            - Say what's in the dir, not what kind of dir it is.
              ("Per-property document folders", not "directory of subdirs")
            - Skip filler ("this is a", "contains", "directory of").

            SHELL DIRS — when a subdir's contents are hidden by ignore
            patterns (e.g. `store/archive/captures/` whose dated capture
            sessions are excluded by `store/archive/captures/*`), the dir
            appears in the parent's listing but its own children list will
            look empty. Peek inside with `ls` to give an honest count and
            characterization, e.g. "captures/ — 143 archived voice/photo
            capture sessions (per-item maps disabled)".

            Use `cb create` or just `Write` to author each MAP.md. Don't
            modify any other files.

            STEP 3 - COMMIT:

            ```bash
            git add -A && git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
            Refresh maps: <N> map(s)

            - <dir1>/MAP.md (<created|updated>)
            - <dir2>/MAP.md (<created|updated>)

            Triggered-By: cb procedure
            Phase: refresh
            EOF
            )"
            ```

            STEP 4 - FINALIZE:
            ```
            cb refresh-maps --finalize
            ```
            This adds an `@MAP.md` line to each affected directory's CLAUDE.md
            (creating a stub if it doesn't exist), stamps the state file at
            HEAD, and prunes entries for deleted directories. Don't commit
            after — the procedure engine's "Complete step" commit sweeps
            those file changes into the same step commit.

            GIT: Do NOT add Co-Authored-By to commits. The system adds the
            appropriate trailers automatically.
          model: haiku
          max-turns: 40
    validate:
      shells:
        - >-
          # If --brief still reports needsWork=true, the agent missed something.

          # Use --brief (not the bare command) so we don't re-save the brief
          file.

          output=$(cb refresh-maps --brief 2>/dev/null || true)

          if echo "$output" | grep -q '"needsWork": true'; then
            echo "WARNING: cb refresh-maps --brief still reports outstanding work."
            echo "$output" | head -40
            exit 1
          fi

          echo "All MAP.md files current."
      instructions:
        - |-
          After the agent runs, the next precheck should be a no-op
          (needsWork=false). If it still reports tasks, the agent missed
          one or more — re-run the procedure or inspect manually.
      whys:
        - |-
          If a dirty MAP.md is silently missed, state stamping will move
          the asOf forward and future precheck runs won't notice the
          stale listing.
      severity: abort
---
